<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{{.ProjectName}} — web</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>{{.ProjectName}}</h1>
      <p>
        The same engine the CLI links, running here as a wasip2 component with
        its filesystem bound to OPFS — so this page, the CLI, and the
        <a href="/terminal.html" data-testid="terminal-link">in-page terminal</a>
        all drive the same handlers. The terminal has every command in
        <code>commands.proto</code>, including inherited ones this page has no
        button for.
        The <a href="/files.html" data-testid="files-link">files</a> page shows
        what is actually in OPFS.
        <a href="/commands.html" data-testid="commands-link">commands</a> lists
        every command with its flags, straight from the schema.
      </p>
      <input id="name" value="ILC" />
      <button id="greet" data-testid="greet">greet</button>
      <pre id="out" data-testid="out"></pre>
    </main>
    <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
